{
  "title": "Users and Roles: Manage Access, Names and Avatars | CrestApps for Orchard Core",
  "description": "Every person who signs in has a user account, and a role decides what that person can do. Giving each person a long list of permissions is slow and easy to get wrong, and screens that show only sign-in names are hard to read. Users and roles give you access that is simple to manage, with names and pictures people recognize.\n\nIn this video:\n• Why users and roles\n• How users, roles, permissions, names and avatars fit together\n• Reading the user list, and searching, filtering and sorting it\n• Adding a person with a password and roles\n• Creating a role and choosing its permissions\n• Giving a person a role\n• Choosing how names appear, with first and last names\n• Avatars, and signing in with an emailed code\n• Four ways to use it",
